CM This illustrates a vertical antenna with elevated radial
CM system. At 0.0001 wavelength, the height is about as low
CM as NEC can model accurately. 
CM Calculated performance does largely depend on the position
CM of the excitation source related to the radiator lenght,
CM the distance from the radial wires connection and their 
CM lengths.
CE
SY freq=14.35	'frequency (MHz)
SY WL=299.8/freq	'wave length
SY M=WL/1000	'minimum NEC segment length
SY len=35.56	'length
SY radh=0.01778	'radial height
SY radl=39.624	'radial length
GW	1	3	0	0	radh	0	0	radh+3*M	0.0012941	'Short wire for excitation source
GW	2	70	0	0	radh+3*M	0	0	len	0.0012941	'Rest of radiatior.
GW	0	55	0	0	radh	radl	0	radh	0.0012941	'Radial wires
GW	0	55	0	0	radh	0	radl	radh	0.0012941
GW	0	55	0	0	radh	-radl	0	radh	0.0012941
GW	0	55	0	0	radh	0	-radl	radh	0.0012941
GE	-1
GN	2	0	0	0	13	0.005
EK
EX	0	1	2	0	1	0	0	0
FR	0	0	0	0	freq	0
EN
